  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 589a77387c7c4ea488d9368fe6c3cd2f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Sub Dialogue 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  characterName: Axion
  dialogues:
  - Great job! Now that you have your initial embedding and your ATTENTION embedding,
    you can add them together. This is called a RESIDUAL CONNECTION. This ensures
    that information that was encoded in previous embeddings isn't lost in the sauce!
  - However, because you are adding two embeddings together, the numbers tend to
    grow. This can quickly bloat the numbers when coupled with multiplication and
    addition later on in the model. To counteract this, it is standard to NORMALIZE
    your embedding after addition.
  - NORMALIZING will scale the numbers down so the mean falls around 0 and the standard
    deviation becomes 1, without changing the distribution of the numbers.
  - Add your POSITIONAL ENCODER embedding and ATTENTION embedding together and NORMALIZE
    the result!
